{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Upon which the splatter falls — you shall wash.</b> And not the entire garment requires washing." "<b>You shall wash.</b> Because the blood is the blood of a hata'at whose meat is eaten inside the curtains, and if some of its blood splatters on a garment and goes outside the curtains, it is disqualified by going out." "<b>In a holy place.</b> To include chambers built in non-sacred space and opening into the sacred area."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:20.494424523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}